Hardware-Aware Dynamic Scheduling for Multicore Systems

A userspace Linux scheduling framework that uses runtime hardware performance counters to classify workloads and dynamically optimize multicore CPU placement.

🎯 Overview

Traditional Linux scheduling primarily focuses on fairness and CPU utilization without directly considering the hardware behavior of individual workloads.

This project implements a hardware-aware adaptive scheduling framework that continuously profiles running processes using Linux hardware performance counters and dynamically adjusts CPU placement based on workload behavior.

The framework operates entirely in userspace, without modifying the Linux kernel scheduler.

